<%# What goes inside the frame's <main> for a page, and nothing else (theming
    spec §2): the head tags that describe the page (pages/_seo_meta) and the
    preview bar are rendered by the layout, so a theme that replaces this
    file cannot lose either. %>
<%# The page is drawn by its template (`page_template`: the page's stored
    template while the theme declares it, the theme's first otherwise), each
    a partial `pages/templates/_<name>.html.erb` handed the three locals a
    template is promised: the page shown, the post on a post's own detail
    view, and the list block that post was found under. This file ends with no
    line break after the render, so the page ends where the template does. %>
<%= render "pages/templates/#{page_template}", page: @page, post: @post, list_block: @post_list_block %>